# =================================================================
# QWEN 3.6 35B A3B (mudler APEX-MTP-I-Compact) - 2 SLOTS - CUDA MODE
# =================================================================
# Concurrent counterpart to the APEX-I-Mini single-slot profile. Two 128K slots
# at 64.28 +/- 1.2 tok/s -- 42% above the old 2-slot default's 45.14.
#
# WHY I-Compact HERE AND I-Mini FOR ONE SLOT: the ranking between the two APEX
# quants inverts with concurrency, measured n=5 each:
#   1 slot  (ctx 131072):  I-Mini 79.11  >  I-Compact 75.74
#   2 slots (ctx 262144):  I-Compact 64.28  >  I-Mini 58.62
#   3 slots (ctx 393216):  I-Mini 51.62
# I-Mini also becomes noticeably noisier once a second slot exists
# (+/-3.4, samples 55.5-62.7) while I-Compact stays tight (+/-1.2), so Compact
# is both faster and steadier here. I-Compact is also the less aggressive quant
# (17.3GB vs 14.3GB), which is extra insurance on harder prompts.
#
# Same Qwen3.6-35B-A3B MoE weights as the champion -- verified from GGUF
# metadata: identical architecture (qwen35moe), identical tensor count (753),
# 41 blocks, 256 experts, 8 routed per token, license pointing at
# Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B. Quantized with per-expert precision (APEX) rather than
# uniformly. MTP head bundled and verified active in the server log
# ("common_speculative_init_result: creating MTP draft context").
#
# CAVEAT: the APEX files carry no base_model provenance metadata and their
# general.name is the placeholder "Safetensors", so the base cannot be verified
# from the file alone -- only the architecture, which a fine-tune would share.
# Behavioural evidence is good (10/10 on the LRU-cache-with-TTL suite).
COMPOSE_FILE=docker/alternatives/docker-compose-gpu-qwen-35b-a3b-apex-compact-2slot.yml

HF_REPO="mudler/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-APEX-MTP-GGUF"
HF_FILE="Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-APEX-MTP-I-Compact.gguf"

# Local host to access llama-server
LLAMA_HOST=127.0.0.1
# Local port to access llama-server
LLAMA_PORT=12345

# Total context across all slots (2 slots x 131072 = 262144)
LLAMA_CONTEXT_SIZE=262144

# CPU Threads (total threads - 2)
LLAMA_CPU_THREADS=14

# Local storage path for GGUF model files
MODELS_DIR=""
